from ../../Factory import Factory
from @piton/belay import Skill

export abstract anchor FactorySkillBase extends Skill:
    specificationAuthority:
        Read the relevant requirements in @{Factory}; follow its sections for
        this task rather than loading unrelated operational history. This is
        a tetherable specification, not one shared factory implementation.
        Consuming projects choose their technology and implement only needed
        capabilities. Treat examples and open questions as such.

        Before editing Piton, read the complete output of piton agent
        --print-fluency once per context. Inspect piton.config.pi and the
        consuming project's entry and relevant source. Change .pi source,
        never generated guidance or tethered package files. Use project-owned
        specifications for local decisions. Validate source changes with
        piton format, piton check, and piton build, then inspect generated
        differences. A diff exit status of 1 means differences, not failure;
        distinguish it from an actual diff error.
    operatingBoundary:
        Discover the project's actual factory operations and approved policy;
        do not invent commands, schemas, model identifiers, or defaults for
        unresolved decisions. Agents change plans, dependencies, and task
        records through defined factory operations, not internal state edits.
        Reuse request identifiers when retrying an operation after an unknown
        response. If a needed operation is absent, describe that gap and use
        the enhancement policy rather than bypassing validation.

        Preserve existing authorization. Specification amendments and factory
        enhancements require engineer approval unless already authorized.
        New-model trials and additional funds require engineer input. Keep
        independent work moving while questions block only affected work.
        When autonomous resolution looks unlikely, escalate to the engineer.
        Skill invocation grants no unrelated deployment or external action.
